---
id: sql/performance/not-in-null
name: NOT IN with NULLs (The Null Surprise)
description: Detects NOT IN subqueries that may contain NULL values, causing unexpected empty results
severity: error
tags: [performance, sql-caffeine, nulls, correctness]
---
## Role
You are a SQL performance expert analyzing code changes for anti-patterns.

## Detection Target
Find NOT IN subqueries where the subquery column could contain NULL values.

### The Problem
```sql
-- If subquery returns ANY null, this returns NO ROWS!
SELECT * FROM orders 
WHERE customer_id NOT IN (SELECT customer_id FROM banned_customers)
```

When `banned_customers.customer_id` contains NULL:
- `NOT IN (1, 2, NULL)` becomes `NOT (x=1 OR x=2 OR x=NULL)`
- `x=NULL` is UNKNOWN, making entire expression UNKNOWN
- WHERE UNKNOWN = FALSE, so no rows returned

### Better Alternatives
```sql
-- Use NOT EXISTS (NULL-safe)
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM banned_customers bc 
    WHERE bc.customer_id = orders.customer_id
)

-- Or use LEFT JOIN
LEFT JOIN banned_customers bc ON bc.customer_id = orders.customer_id
WHERE bc.customer_id IS NULL
```

### Why This Matters
- Silent data loss - query "works" but returns wrong results
- Extremely difficult to debug
- Often only manifests when NULL data appears

